                <pb facs="0784" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/119: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-18T17:00:00-03:00">January 18, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 18—4:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Your 6, January 17, 4 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs has only replied with
                    generalities in conversation. Today he expressed surprise that I had not yet
                    received his written reply to my notes and said it would be delivered without
                    delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
